From abe71efb9bd148e9761feb95a443e99fd2944a87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:10:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: authored 3D subtitle depth for MVC remuxes

The plane offset metadata a 3D Blu-ray authors for its subtitles
travels in the SEI of the MVC dependent view, so an MKV remux of the
disc carries it too; only the playlist's STN-SS table, which says
which offset sequence each PG stream follows, is lost with the disc
structure. Read the metadata on the ffmpeg demuxer side as well:

- ParseOffsetMetadataAvcc() walks the length-prefixed (ISO 14496-15)
  access units a remux carries, beside the Annex-B parser.
- CDVDDemuxFFmpeg owns a COffsetMetadataStore for an H.264 stream it
  has detected as multiview, feeds it from each dependent-view access
  unit with the packet pts and 1/fps, flushes it with the demuxer and
  clears it with the streams. A one-shot log says whether offsets were
  found or, after 120 access units, that there are none.
- CVideoPlayer takes the demuxer's store when the input is not a
  Blu-ray, and maps PG stream n to offset sequence n, which is how
  MakeMKV keeps the disc's order: measured on Hugo and Coraline.
  Only the main demuxer's PGS streams count, so an external subtitle
  file or a muxed-in text track cannot shift the numbering.

Tested with MakeMKV remuxes on a Radeon RX 7600 driving a JVC
DLA-RS4100 in frame packing: the Hugo remux reports 32 sequences and
its subtitles move shot by shot exactly as from the ISO of the same
disc; a title without dependent-view offsets is unaffected.

Hades: adapted to this tree, which tells an MVC track of a Matroska file by its own
rule (KODI::MULTIVIEW::TwoViews() in AddStream(): the private data names a second
view, the videoplayer.hades3dmvc setting allows it, the h264_mvc decoder is built and
the container names no other layout). The store is configured there, for a track that
is to be decoded as two views and for no other: a remux whose base view plays alone,
as with no 3D display, has no store and takes the path it took before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
